Contributing to ProjT Launcher
==============================

Contributor License Agreement (CLA)
-----------------------------------

By submitting a contribution to this repository, you agree that your
contribution is made under the terms of the Project Tick Contributor
License Agreement (CLA).

The CLA ensures that:

you have the legal right to submit the contribution,
the contribution does not knowingly infringe third-party rights,
Project Tick may distribute the contribution under the applicable
  Project Tick license(s) governing the component,
long-term governance and license consistency across the Project Tick
  ecosystem can be maintained.

The CLA applies to all intentional contributions, including but not
limited to source code, documentation, tests, data, media assets, and
configuration files.

The full text of the current CLA is available at:

<https://projecttick.org/licenses/PT-CLA-2.0.txt>

If you do not agree to the CLA, please do not submit contributions.

----------------------------------------------------------

Quick Start
-----------

in Windows:

git clone https://github.com/Project-Tick/ProjT-Launcher.git
cd ProjT-Launcher
.\configure.bat --with-tests --platform=windows --shared
make

in Linux or macOS

git clone https://github.com/Project-Tick/ProjT-Launcher.git
cd ProjT-Launcher
./configure --with-tests --shared
make

----------------------------------------------------------

Requirements
------------

| Component |         Requirement       |
| --------- | ------------------------- |
| GNU Make  | Latest Version            |
| Qt        | 6.8.6+                    |
| Compiler  | C++23 support             |
| Python    | 3.9+ (for metadata tools) |

----------------------------------------------------------

Project Areas
-------------

launcher/           Launcher application (C++/Qt)
meta/               Metadata generator (Python)
docs/               Documentation
ci/, .github/       CI/CD and automation
scripts/, tools/    Build and development tools

Fork Libraries
**************

These are independently maintained forks:

zlib/                   Compression library (if you want contribute in this subsystem please go to
                                            https://git.projecttick.org/pub/scm/Project-Tick/zlib.git)
bzip2/                  Compression library 
quazip/                 ZIP archive handling
cmark/                  Markdown parsing (if you want contribute in this subsystem please go to
                                          https://git.projecttick.org/pub/scm/Project-Tick/cmark.git)
tomlplusplus/           TOML parsing (if you want contribute in this subsystem please go to
                                      https://git.projecttick.org/pub/scm/Project-Tick/tomlplusplus.git)
libqrencode/            QR code generation (if you want contribute in this subsystem please go to
                                            https://git.projecttick.org/pub/scm/Project-Tick/libqrencode.git)
libnbtplusplus/         NBT format support
extra-cmake-modules/    CMake utilities (if you want contribute in this subsystem please go to
                                        https://git.projecttick.org/pub/scm/Project-Tick/extra-cmake-modules.git)
gamemode/               GameMode integration
LocalPeer/              Single instance support
murmur2/                Hash functions
qdcss/                  Dark CSS support
rainbow/                Terminal colors
systeminfo/             System information

----------------------------------------------------------

Code Style
----------

This is a summary. See docs/contributing/CODE_STYLE.md for full rules.

C++ (clang-format)
******************

IMPORTANT:
Please use LLVM 19 to format files.

clang-format -i path/to/file.cpp

Key rules:

Tabs for indentation (width: 4)
Column limit: 120
Allman brace style
C++23 standard
C11 or C23 standard

Commit Messages
***************

what do you do in this repository: short description

Optional explanation of what and why.

Examples:

fix: fix crash on startup with invalid config

----------------------------------------------------------

DCO Sign-off
------------

The DCO is used as a technical attestation
mechanism and does not replace or weaken the
CLA.

Every commit must include a sign-off line:

git commit -s -m "what do you do in this repository: description"

This adds:

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>

The bot enforces DCO compliance and labels PRs missing sign-off.

----------------------------------------------------------

Mailing List Process
--------------------

Before Submitting
*****************

Run clang-format on changed files
Ensure code compiles without warnings
Add tests for new functionality
Sign off all commits
Update documentation if needed

How to Send Mail to the Mailing List
************************************

Generate patches with git format-patch, then send them with git send-email.
Replace the address with the actual mailing list.

git format-patch -n(Enter the number of commits you want to send.) --cover-letter

eg.

git format-patch -n1 --cover-letter

Please edit 0000-cover-letter.patch to add description in this patch.

Add CC recipients from the maintainers list:
make maintainer-emails
git send-email --to mailing-list@example.org --cc (make maintainer-emails) 000*.patch

Configure SMTP for git send-email (example):
git config --global sendemail.smtpServer smtp.example.org
git config --global sendemail.smtpServerPort 587
git config --global sendemail.smtpEncryption tls
git config --global sendemail.smtpUser you@example.org
git config --global sendemail.from "Your Name <you@example.org>"

ML Requirements
***************

Clear description of what and why
Reference related issues
Pass all CI checks
One logical change per ML
Do not mix: refactors, features, and third-party updates must be in separate MLs
Third-party library updates require standalone MLs with documented rationale

Review Process
**************

1. Maintainer reviews code
2. Address feedback
3. Merge when approved

----------------------------------------------------------

Testing
-------

Running Tests
*************

make test

Writing Tests
*************

- Use QtTest framework
- Test public interfaces
- Mock external dependencies
- Cover edge cases

----------------------------------------------------------

Architecture
------------

The launcher follows MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel) pattern:

Model       Data and business logic
ViewModel   Presentation logic, state management
View        Qt Widgets UI components

MVVM is enforced conceptually. UI classes launcher/ui/ must not contain business logic—only presentation and user interaction. See docs/contributing/ARCHITECTURE.md for full design guidance.

